### 1. Health Check
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### 2. API Documentation
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

### 3. Swagger UI
GET http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html

### 4. Register New User
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123",
  "roles": ["USER"],
  "active": true
}

### 6. Login with Test User
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}

###LOGIN WRONG USERNAME
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "wronguser",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Register Admin User
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123",
  "roles": ["ADMIN"],
  "active": true
}



### 7. Login with Admin User
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 8. Get All Users (Requires Authentication)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token_here>

### 9. Get User by ID (Requires Authentication)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token_here>

### 10. Get User by Username (Requires Authentication)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/username/testuser
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token_here>

### 11. Update User (Requires Authentication)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token_here>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "updateduser",
  "password": "newpassword123",
  "roles": ["USER"],
  "active": true
}

### 12. Delete User (Requires Admin Role)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/2
Authorization: Bearer <your_admin_jwt_token_here>

### 13. Test Unauthorized Access (Should return 403)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### 14. Test Invalid Login (Should return 401)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nonexistent",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 15. Test H2 Console (if enabled)
GET http://localhost:8080/h2-console